  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Suresh Chand Chaurasiya vs State Of M.P. on 5 May, 2016 1 M.Cr.C. No. 26/2011 High Court Of Madhya Pradesh Bench Gwalior Miscellaneous Criminal Case No. 26/2011 Suresh Chand Chaurasiya (died, name deleted) and two others Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh through Shri S.S. Kushwaha, Food Inspector For the applicant : Shri R.K. Sharma, Advocate For the State : Shri Mohd. Irshad, Panel Lawyer Present :",
    "facts": "The applicants have also challenged the order dated 19.08.2010 passed by the JMFC, Gwalior. (2) Facts of the case, in short, are that the respondent- Food Inspector had lodged a criminal complaint against the applicants and other accused persons that on 27.02.1992 at 05:00 PM, he inspected the shop of applicant No. 3 Shankarlal and sons and inspected the sealed packets of Bhola Chhap Jafrani Patti Tobacco having 50 gm tobacco in each packet and thereafter the proceeding of seizure was started. Sample was sent for analysis and thereafter getting the report from Public Analyst, the complaint was filed. The trial Court has framed the aforesaid charges vide order dated 19.08.2010.",
    "arguments": "the light of the judgment passed by the Apex Court in case of \"Smt. Manibai and another Vs. State of Maharashtra\" [AIR 1974 SC 434], the sleeping partner could not be prosecuted for offence of food adulteration done by the partnership firm.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "the light of the judgment passed by the Apex Court in case of \"Smt. Manibai and another Vs. State of Maharashtra\" [AIR 1974 SC 434], the sleeping partner could not be prosecuted for offence of food adulteration done by the partnership firm."
  },
